# Frontend Standards

## Stack

- React + Next.js App Router + TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS with design tokens in `globals.css`
- shadcn/ui for primitives; Framer Motion for section entrance only
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed

## Architecture

- Modular components under `src/components/` — one concern per file
- Marketing sections in `src/components/marketing/<name>-section.tsx`
- Shared layout in `src/components/layout/`; motion wrappers in `src/components/motion/`
- Composition over prop drilling; use `cn()` for class merging

## HTML & Accessibility (WCAG)

- Semantic elements: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `footer`, proper heading order
- All interactive elements keyboard accessible with visible `:focus-visible` rings
- Labels for inputs; `aria-label` when no visible label; `sr-only` for screen-reader text
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; do not block zoom (`maximumScale: 1` is forbidden)
- Body text contrast ≥ 4.5:1; large text ≥ 3:1

## UI States (required for interactive blocks)

- Default, hover, focus, active, disabled
- Loading, empty, and error states for async or data-driven UI

## Design

- Mobile-first responsive layouts; test at 320px, 768px, 1280px
- Consistent spacing (4px grid); use `Section` for vertical rhythm
- Minimalist interfaces; avoid clutter; clear visual hierarchy
- Subtle animations only; CSS for micro-interactions, Framer for scroll reveals

## Nielsen Heuristics Checklist

Before shipping UI, verify: visibility of status, real-world match, user control, consistency, error prevention, recognition over recall, flexibility, aesthetic minimalism, error recovery, help/documentation where needed.

## Pre-ship Review

Evaluate every change for: accessibility, responsiveness, visual hierarchy, usability, consistency, maintainability, and Nielsen compliance.
